<section>
  <h2>Why sector specialisation matters</h2>
  <p>A guard trained for a manufacturing gatehouse will not naturally know how to handle a distressed family at a hospital ICU. A retail-mall guard who's never worked a wedding doesn't know how to brief a bouncer team for a 2,000-guest function. We don't pretend a guard is interchangeable — we deploy people trained for the site they will work at.</p>
  <p>For every sector listed above, we have:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>A sector-specific induction module with role-play scenarios.</li>
    <li>A supervisor with sector experience as the first escalation contact.</li>
    <li>Equipment and SOP defaults tuned to that sector's risk profile.</li>
    <li>Sample SLAs and incident-reporting templates aligned with sector norms.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
